# Implementation Plan: Sign In with Microsoft (MSAL)

We will integrate native **Microsoft Sign-In** into your Expo React Native app using `react-native-msal` and connect it to your Express/MongoDB backend.

---

## 🔄 Authentication Sequence & Workflow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant App as React Native App (MSAL)
    participant Azure as Microsoft Azure AD
    participant API as Express Backend
    participant DB as MongoDB

    User->>App: Taps "Sign in with Microsoft"
    App->>Azure: Launches MSAL Native Browser / Authenticator Prompt
    User->>Azure: Enters Microsoft Credentials
    Azure-->>App: Redirects to msauth://com.kotav.myfirstapp with Access Token
    App->>App: Fetches Profile (Name, Email, Microsoft ID)
    App->>API: Sends POST /api/auth/microsoft (Name, Email, Microsoft ID)
    API->>DB: Finds or Creates User in MongoDB
    DB-->>API: User Record Returned
    API-->>App: Returns App JWT Session Token
    App->>User: Navigates to Home Dashboard (Displays Name & Email)
```

---

## 📋 Requirements Checklist

### 1. Azure Portal Configuration (User Action)
- Log in to [portal.azure.com](https://portal.azure.com).
- Create an **App Registration**.
- Copy **Application (Client) ID** and **Directory (Tenant) ID**.
- Add **Android Platform** in Azure Portal:
  - **Package Name:** `com.kotav.myfirstapp`
  - **Redirect URI:** `msauth://com.kotav.myfirstapp/<BASE64_SHA1_HASH>`

